# Soft-blue UI chrome

Desktop selection / hover / toolbar-checked chrome uses soft blue, not system highlight.  
**Source of visual truth for shared tokens:** Harrix-HTML-Template `src/scss/_variables.scss`.  
Desktop mirror: `src/harrix_swiss_knife/apps/common/ui_chrome.py`. Table: `.cursor/design-tokens.md`.

| Token | Hex | Role |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `SELECTION_BG` | `#e8f4fc` | Selected fill |
| `SELECTION_BORDER` / `BUTTON_PRIMARY_BG` | `#2e86b7` | Brand / solid primary |
| `SELECTION_HOVER` | `#f3f8fb` | Hover fill |
| `BRAND_INK` / `BUTTON_PRIMARY_HOVER` | `#1a5f7a` | Ink / primary hover |
| `MUTED_TEXT` | `#5c6370` | Secondary labels |
| `INPUT_BORDER` | `#dbdbdb` | Inputs / secondary border |
| `HAIRLINE` | `#f0f0f0` | Light separators |
| `SEPARATOR` | `#e0e0e0` | Row separators |
| `BUTTON_SECONDARY_BG` | `#f5f5f5` | Light secondary / toolbar plate |
| `BUTTON_SUCCESS_BG` | `#4caf50` | Success solid |
| `BUTTON_DANGER_BG` | `#cc584c` | Danger solid |

Also: `LUCIDE_COLOR_BLUE` / caption active tab = `#2e86b7`.

## Buttons

- Primary CTA: solid brand via `button_primary_qss()` — **not** mint/Material soft-fill with a different border color.
- Secondary / toolbar idle: `BUTTON_SECONDARY_*` / `button_secondary_qss()`.
- Prefer helpers in `ui_chrome` over hardcoding button QSS in `.ui` files.

## Rules

- Reuse `ui_chrome` tokens for lists, cards, Quick paste/launcher, toolbar checked, caption accents, CTAs.
- Selected items: soft fill + border, dark text on highlight (`SELECTION_TEXT` / readable palette helper).
- Do not invent a different “brand blue” for chrome.
- Prefer importing tokens over hardcoding `#e8f4fc` / `#2e86b7` / `#1a5f7a` / `#dbdbdb`.
- When changing shared tokens: update HTML `_variables.scss` first, then this file and `.cursor/design-tokens.md`.

## Do not unify

- Screenshot region overlay (`#00AEFF` in `selection_paint.py`) — capture guide, not chrome
- Desktop caption height (32px) / Win11 caption buttons — not site navbar
- Shared CSS package with the website — keep tokens conceptually aligned only
- Site TOC pattern (text + left border) — desktop keeps fill selection
- Per-app *content* accents that are not CTAs (charts, category tags) unless explicitly shared
